Performance Optimization
Query Optimization
dax
-- ❌ Inefficient (iterates all rows)
Slow Measure = 
SUMX(Orders, Orders[TotalAmount] * Orders[Quantity])

-- ✅ Efficient (uses aggregation)
Fast Measure = 
SUM(Orders[TotalAmount]) * 
AVERAGE(Orders[Quantity])
Memory Optimization
Hide unused columns from model
Use integer data types when possible
Apply filters at source when available
Archive old data periodically



Calculation Optimization
dax
-- Use CALCULATE for context changes
Optimized = 
CALCULATE(
    SUM(Orders[TotalAmount]),
    Orders[OrderStatus] = "Completed"
)

-- Avoid FILTER when CALCULATE is available
Unoptimized = 
SUMX(
    FILTER(Orders, Orders[OrderStatus] = "Completed"),
    Orders[TotalAmount]
)



